    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. specifically regarding the testing and staging gates, i'm worried about things slipping through that automated tests might miss. what are some common ways those \"hidden\" issues or edge cases usually bypass the gates we've set up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hidden issues often slip through due to insufficient test coverage in complex integration paths or reliance solely on unit tests which don't cover environment-specific failures. Edge cases are typically missed because test data fails to represent real-world production variability, like peak load or specific user permission combinations. To mitigate this, incorporating chaos engineering practices and running tests against environments that mirror production infrastructure closely is highly recommended.",
      "source": "target",
