      "content": "yeah i get the technical side of it. but from a management perspective, it feels like there's always something \"sneaky\" that manages to get past our security checks or testing gates right when we think everything is solid. how do you describe those kinds of unexpected, disruptive things that just appear in the system and mess up the deployment?",
