      "content": "From a management perspective, those unexpected disruptions are often categorized as systemic risks or emergent behaviors. These are not simple bugs but rather failures in the assumptions made during design or testing, like unforeseen performance bottlenecks under load. It is better to describe them as \"unmodeled variables\" that testing environments failed to capture, requiring proactive shift-left security and operational resilience measures.",
